  {
   "heading": "Commas",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "12edo tempers out the following commas . This assumes val ⟨ 12 19 28 34 42 44 ] ."
  },
  {
   "heading": "Rank-2 temperaments",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "* Octave-reduced form , reduced to the first half-octave, and minimal form in parentheses if distinct"
  },
  {
   "heading": "Octave stretch or compression",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Whether there is intonational improvement from octave stretch and compression for 12edo varies by context. A slight compression such as what is given by 40ed10 and 34zpi shows improved intonation of harmonics 5 and 7 at the cost of worse 2 and 3 , while stretching the octave for a purer 3 and for a better match of the inharmonicity on string instruments, like those in 7edf , 19edt , or 31ed6 , also makes sense."
  },
  {
   "heading": "Scales",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "The two most common 12edo mos scales are meantone[5] and meantone[7]."
  },
  {
   "heading": "Non-mos scales",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "Due to 12edo's dominance, some non-mos scales are also widely used in many musical practices around the world.\nFile:12edo modes.pdf"
  },
  {
   "heading": "Well temperaments",
   "level": 2,
   "text": ""
  },
  {
   "heading": "Music",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "The vast majority of music today is in 12edo or 12edo with slight modifications. As such, one can easily find 12edo music by going on any music streaming service."
  },
